// RUN: cd %corpus && ! %zomc compile --check 08-adt/inherent_method_primitive_member_capability_neg_30.zom > %t 2>&1
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file %t

// A dot member read on a primitive str parameter inside an inherent method
// body is legal syntax the body slice cannot lower. The string-length fold
// only applies to string-literal-initialized locals, so a str parameter stays
// unsupported. Inside a method it drains with the method capability code
// ZOM4125, scoped to the enclosing method, instead of reaching a
// missing-fact invariant.

// CHECK-LITERAL: Error [ZOM4125]: method call `g` is not supported yet
// CHECK-LITERAL:   --> conformance/08-adt/inherent_method_primitive_member_capability_neg_30.zom:5:16
// CHECK-LITERAL:   |
// CHECK-LITERAL: 5 |         return s.length;
// CHECK-LITERAL:   |                ^~~~~~~~
// CHECK-LITERAL: 1 error generated.
